
### submit pushes every branch of the current stack, parents first
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin (new branch)
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a on origin: yes
feat-b on origin: yes
other-x on origin (other stack): none
feat-b upstream: origin/feat-b
feat-a stackPushed == tip: yes
HEAD: feat-b

### submit says which branches were up to date and which it pushed
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
feat-a is up to date on origin
pushed feat-b to origin
done.
[exit 0]

### submit force-pushes over its own last push
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin
pushed feat-b to origin
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a on origin: yes
feat-b on origin: yes

### submit refuses to overwrite a branch someone else pushed to
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
warning: not pushing 'feat-a': 'origin/feat-a' has commits this branch does not include; fetch them and bring them in (or check they can go) first
pushed feat-b to origin
error: submit failed for 1 branch(es): feat-a
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack submit'.
[exit 1]
origin feat-a has their commit: 1
feat-b on origin: yes

### a branch pushed outside git-stack leases against its remote-tracking ref
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to origin
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a on origin: yes

### an unrecorded branch whose remote moved since the last fetch is not pushed
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
warning: not pushing 'feat-a': 'origin/feat-a' has commits this branch does not include; fetch them and bring them in (or check they can go) first
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
error: submit failed for 1 branch(es): feat-a
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack submit'.
[exit 1]
origin feat-a has their commit: 1

### an unrecorded branch is not pushed over commits fetched but not integrated
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
warning: not pushing 'feat-a': 'origin/feat-a' has commits this branch does not include; fetch them and bring them in (or check they can go) first
pushed feat-b to origin (new branch)
error: submit failed for 1 branch(es): feat-a
Deal with the branches warned about above, then re-run 'git stack submit'.
[exit 1]
origin feat-a has their commit: 1

### submit pushes to remote.pushDefault when it is set
$ git stack submit
submitting stack rooted at feat-a
pushed feat-a to fork (new branch)
pushed feat-b to fork (new branch)
done.
[exit 0]
feat-a on fork: yes
feat-a on origin: none

### submit needs a remote
$ git stack submit
error: no remote to push 'feat-a' to; add one with 'git remote add <name> <url>'
[exit 1]

### submit runs from a branch of a stack, not a trunk or an anchor
$ git stack submit
error: 'main' is not in a stack; check out a branch of the stack to submit
[exit 1]
$ git stack submit
error: 'wt-x' is not in a stack; check out a branch of the stack to submit
[exit 1]
